From 895857b7dc27fd0a3230dc0ce3e84a9368f57724 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tumredsun <tumredsun@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:40:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/21] pinctrl: sunxi: Add support for the Allwinner A733 PIO
 and R-PIO

The A733 uses a bank layout with 0x80 byte bank stride starting at
offset 0x80, dlevel fields 4 bit wide, pull registers at offset 0x30
and dedicated IRQ register blocks in the upper part of each bank's
space (CFG + 0x40 .. 0x58, implicit stride 0x80). Add this as a new
SUNXI_PINCTRL_A733_LAYOUT variant, with per-controller IRQ register
bases and strides now carried in the sunxi_pinctrl struct instead of
hardcoded register constants.

The A733 PIO uses the PIO_POW_MOD_SEL/CTL at 0x40/0x48 (like other
chips, non-inverted, so BIAS_VOLTAGE_PIO_POW_MODE_CTL applies).

The R-PIO (PL/PM banks) uses the existing D1 register layout.
